<p><img src="ronphoto.jpg" align="right" hspace="0" width="150"
height="206">Ron Steinbrecher is a HIGH MASTER pistol shooter
from the great state of Pennsylvania. Apart from holding several
individual National Records in conventional pistol, he has set
records and won National Titles with the UltraDot team. Ron is
one of the best all-round pistol shooters in the entire country
and one of the nicest fellows as well.<br>
<br>
With the intention of helping new shooters in the sport, Ron
wrote a series of articles for his local club newsletter on pistol
shooting fundamentals. He graciously took the time to retype and
email each of them to the Bullseye-L forum, where they eventually
became archived on Ed Hall's website.<br>
<br>
<em>Ron contacted me by email to see if I would be interested in
including his writings on the Bullseyepistol.com website. After reading his email, the articles
were uploaded to this site within an hour! Thank you for the fine
work, Ron!<!-- =========ARTICLE ENDS HERE============= --><script>footer()</script></em> </p>
